s adds seven shared finite-group laws identifying their actual compatible count with S intersect(W-S), W=U+V, and applying existing single-tag mean/variance laws to that subset. The final assembly uses actual prime-field Weierstrass subgroups without a zero-target or symmetry assumption. [pcc:unverified]\n\nThe report separately derives a hand interval-intersection estimate with an explicit subgroup-size condition, and a raw whole-level count/collision budget. It clarifies that fixed-height b^3 cost alone does not decide the balanced target. The new query idea is a charged exact block decision via an implicit translated-sum polynomial and interval gcd, followed by witness self-reduction; no implementation/cost bound is claimed. Known multipoint-evaluation theorems still require supplied points/coefficient vectors. The complete algorithm criterion remains unmet. [pcc:unverified]\n\nValidation: focused build and actual-field probe pass; canonical all-source gate audits212 theorems, zero failures and zero trusted-native exceptions. Seven named axiom prints use only standard axioms. No fresh checker/hosted pass. Original failed floor001 is retained; floor002 passes. All three final PDF pages and diagram inspected. Source/prose whitespace check0; archival check2 solely on original compiler-warning spaces. [pcc:unverified]\n\nPCC-20261116-f43793 remains unverified with nine pinned subjects. The owner ledger appends serially to main; all older owner sources/claim subjects and frozen crypto4311/4338/4352 evidence remain untouched. PR19's queued autonomy/outcome lands with this substantive study. No native numerical, paid or qualification execution. Hosted outcomes are pending for this head. [pcc:unverified]\n\n[Report](docs/batch-selector-query-20261116.md), [PDF](docs/batch-selector-query-20261116/report.pdf), [publication boundary](docs/batch-selector-query-20261116/PUBLICATION.md), prospective plan and original raw receipts accompany the source.\n","labels":[],"milestone